 College says students, alumni, faculty, staff, and friends wear orange and blue on the first Friday of every month and may submit photographs and memories to the College.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/about-the-college/college-history/traditions/all-traditions","source_title":"All Traditions - Gettysburg College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The documented cadence is the first Friday of each month; photo submission is optional.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gettysburg-celebration","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Celebration","title":"Turn Spring Work into a Campus Showcase","subtitle":"Students present academic, creative, and service projects","notes":"Browse the spring program by discipline, select several unfamiliar presentations, and ask student presenters specific questions about their process.","short_summary":"One spring event gathers research, creative practice, and community work into a student showcase.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College describes Celebration as an annual spring event where students showcase work in academics, creative endeavors, and service or outreach.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/about-the-college/college-history/traditions/all-traditions","source_title":"All Traditions - Gettysburg College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The College identifies Celebration as an annual spring event; consult the current program for venues and attendance details.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gettysburg-springfest","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Springfest","title":"Close the Term at Stine Lake","subtitle":"A pre-finals weekend of concerts, food, and outdoor play","notes":"Check the current student schedule, gather at Stine Lake for the programmed activities, and keep the weekend compatible with the final week of classes.","short_summary":"The campus marks the approach of term’s end with a programmed weekend around Stine Lake.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College documents Springfest as a weekend before the final week of classes featuring concerts, free food, merriment, and play on Stine Lake.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/about-the-college/college-history/traditions/all-traditions","source_title":"All Traditions - Gettysburg College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The tradition occurs before the last week of classes; event-specific access and timing require the current College schedule.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gettysburg-servo-thanksgiving","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Servo Thanksgiving Dinner","title":"Let Your Professors Serve Thanksgiving","subtitle":"Faculty and staff bring a family-style feast to student tables","notes":"Arrive according to Dining Services guidance, settle in with a table group, and watch faculty and staff swap classroom roles for serving aprons.","short_summary":"Servo becomes a shared Thanksgiving table where College employees serve students the meal.","evidence_claim":"Gettysburg College documents Servo Thanksgiving as a full Thanksgiving dinner shared by students with friends and served by professors; a College history says the tradition has endured for decades.","source_url":"https://www.gettysburg.edu/news/stories?Headline=Servo+Thanksgiving+through+the+decades&id=50ddd100-f5ad-4205-b1af-2388641ad1d9","source_title":"Servo Thanksgiving through the decades - Gettysburg College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2024-11-21","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null